        exam: [.direct("What happened at your lake cabin?", "\"While my family slept, someone pried open the back door, carried out a small gun safe, and left with it on a boat trailer.\""), .direct("What was inside the safe?", "\"Four antique rifles. I have purchase records for them. A week later, two of them were listed at a gun show.\""), .direct("How was {D} connected to the rifles?", "\"A vendor at the gun show said the seller was {D}. A deputy matched the serial numbers on the two rifles to my records.\""), .direct("Please describe your lake cabin.", "\"My family uses the cabin through the summer and on long weekends. We keep a small gun safe in a back closet with four antique rifles that came from my grandparents.\""), .direct("What did you find that morning?", "\"Around six, I found the back door pried open and the safe gone. Boat trailer tracks in the gravel told me someone had carried it out and driven off.\""), .direct("How did you learn about the gun show listing?", "\"A deputy called after a gun show vendor listed two rifles. The deputy matched the serial numbers to the purchase records I had kept, and they matched.\""), .cross("{D} says {D.he} inherited the rifles from a relative, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. But {D} has no estate papers for them. I will say that is what {D} told me.\""), .cross("Are antique rifles like these common?", "\"Not like these. They have serial numbers that match mine.\""), .cross("Did anyone see {D} at your cabin?", "\"No. We were asleep, and nobody saw who came in. I can only say what the vendor told the deputy about who sold the rifles.\""), .cross("Did you ever give {D} permission to have your rifles?", "\"No. I do not know {D}. The rifles were mine, and nobody had my permission to sell or carry them anywhere.\""), .cross("You did not see who carried the safe out, did you?", "\"No. We were asleep. I only know the door was pried, the safe was gone, and the boat trailer tracks led to the road.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took antique rifles from an occupied cabin and sold them.", "A seller of inherited rifles."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. It won't happen again.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had no estate papers for the rifles.", "{DL} sold two rifles within a week of the burglary."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take the rifles from the cabin?", "\"No. I inherited those rifles from a relative. I was never at that cabin or near that lake.\""), .direct("Why did you sell two rifles at the gun show?", "\"I needed money. I sold two to a vendor at the show. I did not know they were stolen.\""), .direct("Do you have papers showing you inherited the rifles?", "\"No. I do not have estate papers. The relative handed them over years ago, and I never asked for any paper.\""), .direct("Walk us through how you came to have the rifles.", "\"A relative of mine passed away, and the rifles came down to me. They were in the relative's closet for many years before they came to me.\""), .direct("Why did you sell two of them at the gun show?", "\"I needed money for rent and bills that month. I took two rifles to a vendor, who offered me cash, and I accepted without looking at paperwork.\""), .direct("What did you do when the deputy contacted you?", "\"I answered every question. I told the deputy the rifles were from my relative, and I showed an estate letter, though it does not list the rifles.\""), .cross("The serial numbers match {V}'s purchase records, don't they?", "\"So they say. I did not check them. I trusted that they were mine.\""), .cross("You have no paper for four antique rifles. Why should the jury believe you?", "\"I do not have anything on paper. I can only tell you the truth.\""), .cross("The serial numbers match the owner's records, don't they?", "\"That is what the deputy told me. I never checked the serial numbers, and I did not know they belonged to anyone else.\""), .cross("You sold two rifles within a week of the burglary, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I sold them at the next gun show. I did not know about the burglary, and I did not think the timing would matter.\""), .cross("You have no estate papers for the rifles, do you?", "\"Not with me. My relative's papers are in a box I have not been able to find. I sold two quickly because I needed the money.\"")],
        openings: ("While {V}'s family slept in a lake cabin, someone pried open the back door and carried out a gun safe with four antique rifles. A week later, two of them were listed at a gun show, and the vendor says {D} was the seller.", "Listen for the defense evidence, which will show that {D} inherited the rifles from a relative, sold two of them in good faith at a gun show, and never knew they had been stolen."),
        closings: ("A burglary at a lake cabin, a gun safe carried out, and two of its rifles sold at a gun show a week later by {D}. The serial numbers match.", "A relative's rifles, handed down years ago with no paper. The State must prove {D} knew the rifles came from {V}'s cabin."),
