        role: "Store clerk",
        exam: [.direct("What did you see at your store?", "\"A pickup was left at the convenience store with a toddler asleep inside. I found the child napping on the seat.\""), .direct("What does the store camera show?", "\"{D} leaving the truck and walking off. The keys were in the cupholder.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I called deputies right away. The child was asleep under a coat and unharmed.\""), .direct("Tell us about your job at the convenience store.", "\"I work the counter at the store. I see people come and go all day, and I notice when a vehicle is parked oddly in front of the window.\""), .direct("What did you notice about the pickup?", "\"A pickup was left in the front spot with the engine off and the keys in the cupholder. I thought the driver had gone for a walk.\""), .direct("What happened when you heard crying?", "\"About five minutes later, I heard crying from the truck. I went out and found a toddler asleep under a coat, now awake and upset, and called for help.\""), .cross("A coat covered the child, didn't it?", "\"Yes. A coat was over the child. It could have been hard to see from the front.\""), .cross("Did {D} look in the back of the truck?", "\"I did not see that. I only saw {D} leave.\""), .cross("How long was the truck at your store?", "\"About forty minutes. I think the truck had been there a while.\""), .cross("Could someone looking in the back have seen the child?", "\"A coat covered most of the child. From the driver's seat you might not see a small child unless you looked into the back seat.\""), .cross("Did {D} say anything to you before leaving?", "\"No. {D} never came into the store. {D} left the truck, walked off, and I did not see {D} again until the deputies showed me the video.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Customer",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did {D} seem to know there was a child in the truck?", "\"Not that I could tell. {D} got out and left quickly, and did not look into the back seat.\""), .direct("Why do you think {D} left so quickly?", "\"I do not know. {D} looked panicked, like something had gone wrong, and walked away without a word.\""), .direct("Did {D} say anything to you or the clerk?", "\"No. {D} did not speak to me or to the clerk. {D} just got out and walked off.\""), .direct("Walk us through what you saw at the store that morning.", "\"I was buying coffee and saw the pickup pull in. I watched the driver step out, and it did not look like anything unusual until later.\""), .direct("How would you describe {D}'s behavior when leaving the truck?", "\"Hurried and nervous. {D} looked around, closed the door, and walked quickly away from the store without looking back at the truck.\""), .direct("Did you see {D} reach into the back of the truck?", "\"No. I did not see {D} touch the back. {D} got out of the driver's side and left, and I did not notice a child at all.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} open the back door of the truck?", "\"No. I did not see that. I only saw {D} get out of the front seat and leave.\""), .cross("Did you see a coat over the child?", "\"I did not see the child at all. I only learned about it afterward.\""), .cross("How far were you from the truck?", "\"About thirty feet. I could see the driver's door clearly, but the back seat was too far away for me to see inside.\""), .cross("Did you hear the child at any point while {D} was there?", "\"No. I did not hear anything while {D} was at the truck. I only heard about the child after the clerk came out.\""), .cross("You did not see inside the truck, did you?", "\"No. I only saw {D} walk away. The truck windows were dark, and I did not see the child until the clerk pointed.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} stole a truck with a child.", "Unaware."),
        allocution: "\"I'm so sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} left the child alone for forty minutes.", "A coat covered the child."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take the pickup from the church lot?", "\"Yes, I took it. The keys were in the cupholder, and I took it on impulse. It was a terrible decision.\""), .direct("Did you know there was a child in the truck?", "\"No. I did not see a child. A coat covered the child, and I never looked in the back seat.\""), .direct("Tell the jury how you came to take the pickup.", "\"I was walking through the church lot, saw the keys inside a pickup, and took it on impulse. I needed a ride, and I was not thinking clearly.\""), .direct("What did you see when you looked in the back?", "\"Nothing but a pile of stuff. I saw a coat and some bags. I did not see a child, and the coat covered everything in the back seat.\""), .direct("Why did you leave the truck at the convenience store?", "\"I heard a noise in the back and got scared that I was doing something serious. I parked at the store and walked off quickly, and I regret that.\""), .direct("What did you do when you found out there was a child in the truck?", "\"I was told by a clerk after I walked away. I ran back, but the clerk was already calling for help, and I stayed until deputies arrived.\""), .cross("You took a truck that was not yours, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I did not think about who might be inside.\""), .cross("You never looked in the back seat, did you?", "\"No. I own that. I will regret that for the rest of my life.\""), .cross("The child was alone for about forty minutes, wasn't the child?", "\"Yes. I did not know the child was there. I feel sick about it. I should have looked, and I think about it constantly.\""), .cross("You took the pickup without anyone's permission, didn't you?", "\"That is true. I took it without asking. I know it was wrong, and I am not denying that part of what happened.\""), .cross("You did not look in the back seat before you drove off, did you?", "\"No, I did not. I should have, and I will regret that for the rest of my life.\"")],
        openings: ("A pickup with a napping toddler was stolen from a church lot and left at a convenience store forty minutes later. {D} was filmed leaving it, and the child was found asleep under a coat, unharmed.", "The defense evidence will establish that {D} took the truck but never saw the child under the coat in the back, and left when a noise in the back frightened {D}."),
        closings: ("A stolen truck, a toddler alone for forty minutes, and {D} walking away from it on camera. A person who takes a vehicle takes responsibility for who is inside.", "A coat over a sleeping child and a driver who never looked in the back. The State must prove {D} knew the child was there."),
        timeline: [(0, "10 a.m.: the truck is taken."), (0, "10:40 a.m.: left at the store."), (0, "10:45 a.m.: the clerk hears crying."), (0, "11 a.m.: the father arrives.")],
        identified: "A store camera.",
        aggravating: ["The victim was particularly vulnerable"],
        mood: .divided,
        impact: "I will never leave her again.",
        doctrines: ["mistakeOfFact"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let kayakLoadTheftV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.kayakLoadTheft",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Eleven Paddleboards Disappear From Beach Rental Shack, Trailer Seen at Dawn", "Resale Listing Shows Boards With Rental Stickers"],
        law: "felonyLarceny",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Took and carried away property valued at $14,000 belonging to {V}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Eleven rental paddleboards vanished from a beach shack's rack on {DATE}. A camera on the neighboring parking lot showed a pickup with a flatbed trailer at dawn. The plate was partly visible. Two weeks later boards with the shack's stickers were listed at a flea market. A seller's booth was registered to {D}. {DL} says {D.he} bought the boards at a closing sale.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Parking Lot Camera", "A pickup and trailer at dawn."), E(.physical, 3, "Boards at Booth", "Boards with the shack's stickers at {D}'s booth."), E(.document, 2, "Booth Registration", "Booth rented by {D}."), E(.statement, 1, "Neighbor", "Saw a trailer at dawn.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Closing Sale", "{DL} says {D.he} bought them at a closing sale."), E(.document, 1, "Cash Receipt", "A handwritten receipt for $2,000.")],
        role: "Beach shack owner",
        exam: [.direct("What happened at your beach shack on {DATE}?", "\"Eleven rental paddleboards vanished from my rack. A neighboring camera shows a pickup with a flatbed trailer at dawn, with the plate partly visible.\""), .direct("What does the booth registration show?", "\"The booth was rented by {D}. My shack's stickers were on the boards.\""), .direct("Please describe your beach shack business.", "\"I rent paddleboards and kayaks at a beach shack. I keep the boards on a rack outside overnight, because the shack is too small to bring them inside.\""), .direct("What did you find that morning?", "\"At about eight, the rack was empty. Eleven rental boards, each worth several hundred dollars, were gone. I called the sheriff, and a neighbor shared a camera clip.\""), .direct("How did you find the boards again?", "\"Two weeks later, a friend sent a photo of boards with my shack's stickers at a flea market. I called the deputy, and we went to the booth.\""), .direct("What did you do after you found the rack empty?", "\"I counted the missing boards, checked the lock and called the sheriff's office. I then walked the lot and asked the neighbor about the trailer.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} bought them at a closing sale, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"A handwritten receipt shows $2,000. That's far less than the boards are worth.\""), .cross("Can you identify the driver on the camera?", "\"No. A pickup and a trailer. The plate is partial.\""), .cross("Did a neighbor see anything?", "\"A neighbor saw a trailer at dawn. Nothing more.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} take the boards?", "\"No. I was not there at dawn. A neighboring camera shows a pickup and trailer, but the plate is only partly visible, and I cannot say whose it is.\""), .cross("Are the stickers a sure sign the boards were yours?", "\"They are my stickers, and the boards matched my inventory. But I cannot say the seller knew they were stolen when buying them.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took paddleboards and sold them at a flea market.", "A seller who bought boards at a closing sale."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. It won't happen again.\"",
        truths: ("{DL}'s receipt was for $2,000, a fraction of the boards' value.", "{DL} could not name the seller."),
        defendant: [.direct("Where did you get the boards?", "\"At a closing sale. I paid $2,000 cash and got a handwritten receipt. I thought it was a good deal.\""), .direct("Did you take boards from the beach shack?", "\"No. I've never been there at dawn. I would never take from a business.\""), .direct("Why were the shack's stickers on the boards?", "\"I didn't notice them. I figured the seller had stickers from past rentals.\""), .direct("Please describe your booth at the flea market.", "\"I rent a booth most weekends and sell whatever I can find. I buy used items in bulk and resell them, and I have done that for years.\""), .direct("How did you come to have the boards?", "\"I heard about a closing sale at a beach rental place. I paid $2,000 cash for eleven boards and got a handwritten receipt for the purchase.\""), .direct("Why did you not notice the shack's stickers?", "\"I noticed them, but I figured the seller was the shop that closed down. I never thought they were from another business.\""), .cross("$2,000 for eleven boards is cheap, isn't it?", "\"Yes. It was a bargain. I didn't ask many questions.\""), .cross("You put the boards on your booth, didn't you?", "\"Yes. In the open. I wasn't hiding.\""), .cross("Your pickup looks like the one on the neighbor's camera, doesn't it?", "\"It is a common kind of pickup. I own a pickup and a trailer, but I was not at that beach at dawn, and I did not take anything.\""), .cross("You cannot name the seller from the closing sale, can you?", "\"No. I paid in cash, and I did not get a name. I know how that sounds, and I wish I had asked for more information.\""), .cross("You could not name the seller at the closing sale, could you?", "\"No. It was a cash deal in a parking lot, and I did not ask for a name. I should have asked for more than a receipt.\"")],
        openings: ("Eleven rental paddleboards vanished from a beach shack's rack, a pickup and trailer were on a nearby camera at dawn, and two weeks later boards with the shack's stickers were at {D}'s flea market booth. The State will show the camera and the booth registration.", "The defense evidence includes a closing sale, a handwritten receipt, and a seller who displayed the boards openly under {D.his} own registered booth."),
        closings: ("Eleven boards gone, a trailer at dawn, and the shack's stickers on boards at {D}'s own booth. The boards were stolen, and {D} sold them.", "A closing sale, a receipt, and a booth in {D}'s own name. The State has not proved {D} took the boards or knew they were stolen."),
        timeline: [(0, "Dawn: the boards are taken."), (0, "8 a.m.: the shack owner finds the rack empty."), (1, "The lot camera is reviewed."), (14, "The boards appear at a flea market."), (15, "Deputies visit the booth.")],
        identified: "A parking lot camera.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["searchSeizure"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let busConverterRingV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.busConverterRing",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Catalytic Converters Cut From Delivery Vans at a Bakery Fleet Lot", "Twelve Vans Hit Overnight"],
        law: "felonyLarceny",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Took and carried away property valued at $27,000 belonging to {V}, a bakery, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Converters were cut from twelve delivery vans at a bakery fleet lot on {DATE}. A saw in {D}'s truck matched the cuts. {DL} says {D.he} is a mechanic.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Saw Marks", "Match {D}'s saw."), E(.video, 2, "Lot Camera", "A truck near the fence."), E(.document, 3, "Scrap Receipts", "Converters sold under {D}'s ID.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Mechanic", "{DL} says {D.he} is a mechanic.")],
        role: "Fleet manager",
        exam: [.direct("What happened at your fleet lot on {DATE}?", "\"Converters were cut from twelve delivery vans overnight. The vans couldn't run until each was repaired.\""), .direct("What tied {DL} to the cuts?", "\"A saw in {D}'s truck matched the saw marks. A lot camera also shows a truck near the fence.\""), .direct("What do the scrap receipts show?", "\"Converters sold under {D}'s ID at a scrap yard.\""), .direct("Please tell us about your job as a fleet manager.", "\"I manage delivery vans for a bakery. I schedule drivers, track maintenance, and I am responsible for the lot where the vans are parked overnight.\""), .direct("What did your drivers find the next morning?", "\"At about six, drivers noticed the exhaust was loud. Converters had been cut out of twelve vans, and fresh saw marks were on the pipes under each one.\""), .direct("How did you tie the cuts to {D}?", "\"A saw found in {D}'s truck matched the cut marks, and scrap yard receipts show converters sold under {D}'s ID shortly after the theft.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} is a mechanic, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"But the marks matched and the scrap sales are in {D}'s name.\""), .cross("Can you read the truck's plate?", "\"Not clearly. It's a truck near the fence.\""), .cross("Do mechanics sell salvage legally?", "\"Yes. Legitimate salvage exists. I can only say these came off our vans.\""), .cross("Can you read the truck's plate on the lot camera?", "\"No. The camera shows a truck near the fence, but I cannot read the plate or tell the driver's face. I only know where it parked.\""), .cross("Is it common for mechanics to sell converters legally?", "\"Yes. Mechanics sell salvaged parts all the time. But {D} sold many converters in a short period, and these twelve vans lost theirs overnight.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Scrap yard clerk",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Do you work at the scrap yard?", "\"Yes. I'm a clerk. I handle sellers daily.\""), .direct("Does {DL} sell to you?", "\"Regularly. Converters and other salvage.\""), .direct("Is that legal?", "\"As far as I know. {D} always has ID and paperwork.\""), .direct("Please tell us about your work at the scrap yard.", "\"I am a clerk at a scrap yard. I weigh parts, check IDs, and pay sellers, and I handle dozens of sellers every week.\""), .direct("How long has {D} sold converters to the yard?", "\"For several years. {D} comes in regularly with converters and other salvaged parts, always with an ID, and I have never had a problem with a sale.\""), .direct("Is selling salvaged converters legal?", "\"As far as I know, yes. We check IDs and keep records. {D} has always sold under a real name, and the paperwork has been in order.\""), .cross("Did {DL} bring in a large amount?", "\"Some weeks more than others. I'd have to check.\""), .cross("Do you check where converters come from?", "\"No. We check the seller's ID, not the source of the part. That is how most yards work, so I cannot say where each one came from.\""), .cross("Can you tell a salvaged converter from one that was cut off a vehicle?", "\"Sometimes, by the cut ends. I did not examine these specific ones closely, so I cannot say which kind they were.\""), .cross("You do not check where each converter came from, do you?", "\"We check for a title or a work order on larger lots. For smaller sales I take the seller's ID and a signature.\""), .cross("You cannot say where {D}'s converters came from, can you?", "\"I cannot. I know {D} sold them and showed ID, and I do not know where {D} got them.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} stole converters.", "A mechanic."),
        allocution: "\"I'm ashamed of it, Your Honor. I want to make it right.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} sold thirty converters in a month.", "{DL} sells salvaged parts legally."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you have a saw in your truck?", "\"I'm a mechanic. I carry a saw for exhaust work every day.\""), .direct("Where did the converters you sold come from?", "\"From salvage jobs. I sell parts I pull from scrapped cars, using my own ID.\""), .direct("Did you cut converters from the vans?", "\"No. I've never been at that lot at night. I wouldn't do that.\""), .direct("What are your duties as a mechanic?", "\"I fix exhaust systems and pull parts from older vehicles. I sell what I pull to scrap yards, and I do it under my own name each time.\""), .direct("How many converters did you sell that month?", "\"About thirty. That is my usual month during busy weeks. They came from salvage jobs, and I keep receipts for most of them.\""), .direct("Where were you the night the converters were cut?", "\"I was at home. I have never been at that lot at night. I do not know anything about the vans or who cut into them.\""), .cross("You sold converters under your own ID, didn't you?", "\"Yes, many times. It's legal. I never sold stolen ones.\""), .cross("Your truck was near the fence, wasn't it?", "\"A truck was. Lots of trucks look alike. I wasn't there.\""), .cross("The saw marks match your saw, don't they?", "\"That is what they say. Plenty of mechanics own the same model, and I never used mine on a delivery van.\""), .cross("You sold thirty converters in one month, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It is normal for my business. I sell under my own ID because I have nothing to hide about where the parts came from.\""), .cross("The cuts on the vans match your saw, don't they?", "\"I understand the marks match. I use that saw on many jobs, and I did not cut any converter from those vans.\"")],
        openings: ("Converters were cut from twelve delivery vans at a bakery fleet lot overnight. A saw in {D}'s truck matched the cut marks, and a scrap yard bought converters under {D}'s ID soon after the theft.", "The defense will point you to a mechanic who carries a saw for the job and sells salvaged parts legally under a real name. Plenty of mechanics own the same tools, and the State must prove which saw made these cuts."),
        closings: ("Twelve vans cut open overnight, a saw that matches the marks, and converters sold under {D}'s ID. The marks, the saw, and the sales all point to {D}, and the trail does not lead anywhere else.", "A mechanic owns a saw and sells salvage under a real name. The State has not proved the converters came from those vans, and a common tool and legal sales are not proof of theft."),
        timeline: [(-30, "Sales begin."), (0, "Night: the cuts."), (0, "6 a.m.: drivers find them."), (5, "The search.")],
        identified: "Saw marks and receipts.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let truckStopRigTheftV1 = SmallCases.make(
