        openings: ("Roof trusses worth $16,000 were taken from a new subdivision lot, and a site camera photographed a dented flatbed. {D}'s flatbed has a matching dent, and {D} billed a customer for trusses stamped with the site's marks.", "The defense case is that a real customer hired {D} to haul trusses, paid cash, and that {D} did not know where the trusses came from."),
        closings: ("A dented flatbed on camera, trusses with the site's own stamps, and an invoice in {D}'s name. These pieces match one another too well to be a coincidence.", "A hauler who delivered trusses for a customer and was paid in cash. The State must prove {D} knew they were stolen."),
        timeline: [(0, "9 p.m.: the flatbed."), (0, "Midnight: loaded."), (1, "The builder counts."), (3, "The stamps match.")],
