        defendant: [.direct("Whose hives did you move?", "\"My own. I keep hives and I moved some that week. I didn't take any from the orchard.\""), .direct("Why was your smoker at the orchard?", "\"I may have left it there earlier. I visited the orchard before, on friendly terms.\""), .direct("Did you steal {V}'s hives?", "\"No. I'm a beekeeper. I'd never steal another beekeeper's hives.\""), .direct("Please tell us about your beekeeping.", "\"I have kept bees for many years and I sell hives each spring. I know my boxes well, and I repainted four of them recently.\""), .direct("Why would you move hives near the orchard?", "\"I moved some of my own hives for pollination work. I visited the orchard before, and I may have left the smoker there on an earlier trip.\""), .direct("What do you say about the registry showing forty hives to {V}?", "\"I did not take hives registered to anyone else. The hives I moved were mine, and I can show how I raised and painted them.\""), .cross("Forty hives is a lot to move, isn't it?", "\"Yes. Not something one person does in an hour.\""), .cross("Your truck looks like the one on camera, doesn't it?", "\"It's common. I wasn't there that night.\""), .cross("The smoker has your initials, doesn't it?", "\"Yes, it is mine. I carry it to every job, and I have lost tools in fields before. That is why I cannot say when it was left.\""), .cross("You sold hives to the orchard owner before, didn't you?", "\"Yes, a few. That is how I know the owner. It does not mean I took any hives, and I have never taken another beekeeper's boxes.\""), .cross("The hives were registered to {V}, weren't they?", "\"Yes. I sold {V} some earlier and the registry may not show what came back to me. I repainted four boxes, and I have my own marks.\"")],
        openings: ("Forty beehives registered to {V} were taken from an orchard before bloom. A smoker with {D}'s initials was left in the grass, and a camera shows a truck at night. The State will show the smoker and the registry.", "The defense will point you to a beekeeper who owns hives, a fellow beekeeper who knows tools get left behind, and a smoker that was dropped earlier."),
        closings: ("Forty hives gone before bloom, a smoker with {D}'s initials left in the grass, and a truck at the orchard at night. {D} knew the orchard from earlier sales and knew where the hives stood.", "A smoker can be lost on any visit, and a beekeeper's tools get left in fields all the time. The State has not proved {D} took forty hives, and {D} says the hives {D} moved were {D.his} own."),
